WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.779 --> 00:00:03.067
- [Narrator] This is the
gallito de las rocas,

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:06.542
the Andean cock-of-the-rock,
also known as “Tunki”

00:00:06.542 --> 00:00:10.046
in the indigenous language of Quechua.

00:00:10.046 --> 00:00:12.371
Widely-regarded as the
national bird of Peru,

00:00:12.371 --> 00:00:14.564
the gallito de las rocas is native

00:00:14.564 --> 00:00:17.217
to the Andean cloud forests.

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:21.620
Their most distinct feature
is their beautiful feathers.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.221
While the male has a large crest

00:00:23.221 --> 00:00:25.512
and bright orange plumage, the female

00:00:25.512 --> 00:00:27.609
is more modest than its counterpart,

00:00:27.609 --> 00:00:30.009
with darker-brown feathers.

00:00:30.009 --> 00:00:31.850
The brilliant colors help the males

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:34.995
stand out when courting
for a female partner.

00:00:34.995 --> 00:00:37.591
At breeding time, males bob up and down

00:00:37.591 --> 00:00:40.120
hopping around displaying their charms.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.654
Females watch from branches nearby.

00:00:42.654 --> 00:00:44.827
Their feathers have
been an attractive prey

00:00:44.827 --> 00:00:48.294
for the black market,
driving the population down.

00:00:48.294 --> 00:00:50.600
Because of droughts associated
with climate change,

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.358
as well as the massive
destruction of forests,

00:00:53.358 --> 00:00:55.330
the future of their longtime home

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.219
is now being threatened.

00:00:57.219 --> 00:01:00.180
This is the gallito de las rocas.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.930
(uplifting background music)

